= Neurorobotics Group --- Research Projects
[https://www.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/ Department of Computer Science], [https://uni-freiburg.de/ University of Freiburg]

== Current projects

~~~
{}{img_left}{img/projects/carl_zeiss_stiftung.svg}{carl_zeiss_stiftung}{180px}{}{}

/Responsible and Scalable Learning for Robots Assisting Humans (ReScaLe)/

The [https://www.carl-zeiss-stiftung.de/en/project-overview/detail/responsible-and-scalable-learning-for-robots-assisting-humans ReScaLe Project] has multiple goals.
To begin with, robots should be able to learn from observing demonstrations given by humans without having to retrain them completely.
Robots should also be able to transfer policies to new environments by meta-learning on a set of environments.
At the same time, the focus is on responsible development of AI and AI-based robotic systems that are based on human rights.
Finally, the successful mutual transfer of knowledge from scientific to non-scientific actors and vice versa needs to be ensured.

Funded by: [https://www.carl-zeiss-stiftung.de/en/ Carl-Zeiss-Stiftung]
~~~

~~~
{}{img_left}{img/projects/bosch.svg}{bosch}{180px}{}{}

/Planning for Autonomous Driving/

Under the [https://www.bosch.com/de/forschung/aktuelles/gemeinsame-forschung-mit-universitaet-freiburg/ Bosch collaboration with the University of Freiburg], we are a part of the cluster Planning for Autonomous Driving performing research on scene criticality estimation, joint prediction and planning and uncertainty-aware planning.

Funded by: [https://www.bosch.com/en Bosch]
